WEBVTT

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:09.770
The marriage between the sweet 
potatoes and thick miso soup!

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:14.000
I want more!

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.110
What about you, Yushi-kun?

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:17.200
I'm fine.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.780
If you don't eat, you won't 
do well on your tests.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:20.820
Yeah.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.050
Master!

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:26.360
If you need us, you can always 
count on the Petits!

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.240
What could Cait Sith or Chokmah do?

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:34.550
You could burn the answer sheets, 
blow them away, or soak them.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:37.330
That means you would get a make-up test.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:38.830
I see...

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:40.510
I can't do that!

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:44.510
Please quell your anger, master!

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:19.740
<b>Twenty-second Haunting 
Burning Student Assembly!</b>

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:23.960
<i>Damn it... What was the answer?</i>

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:26.860
Master, do you want to burn it?

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:28.370
Shut up.

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:35.490
How did it go, Ta-ko?

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.990
Terrible...

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:40.170
I can't believe we have to 
do this again tomorrow!

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:41.640
What's wrong?

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:42.980
Huh? Seriously?

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:55.610
Chiaki?

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:00.620
<i>That's Nishiyama, from Class E isn't it?</i>

00:03:03.990 --> 00:03:04.990
Ta-ko!

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:07.390
Yon-chan? What happened?

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:10.030
Nishiyama was cheating with his phone!

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:14.590
When the test was half-over...

00:03:19.330 --> 00:03:19.960
Hey!

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:23.930
No, it's nothing.

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:24.680
Sorry.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:28.920
Nishiyama has been rumored 
to be cheating for a while.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:32.050
So everyone knew he'd been caught.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:34.400
But Nishiyama...

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:38.940
He tried to run?

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:39.850
What an idiot.

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:42.270
And then, Chiaki-sensei said...

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:43.850
Nishiyama!

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:50.890
I've never seen a man freeze in place before!

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:53.370
Chiaki-chan's so cool!

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:57.540
He was really scary.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:04:02.970
I was kind of shocked to realize 
that he can look like that.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.450
Actually...

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.420
When he was going down the hall,

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:09.200
he looked sterner than I'd ever seen.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:12.570
He always seems really relaxed.

00:04:13.510 --> 00:04:14.600
That scared me.

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:17.020
<i>Naturally...</i>

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:21.220
<i>He was letting students 
keep their smartphones,</i>

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:23.780
<i>and they basically betrayed him.</i>

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:26.610
<i>Of course he'd be mad.</i>

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:30.780
<i>And no one shows only one side of himself.</i>

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:34.120
<i>Yes, like Ryu-san...</i>

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:37.810
<i>He's always elegant and kind.</i>

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:42.480
<i>I've never seen him angry or even yell.</i>

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.070
<i>But when he said,</i>

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:48.000
<i>"But I offer no help to those 
who refuse to try,"</i>

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:52.560
<i>his eyes were so strict, I shivered.</i>

00:04:53.110 --> 00:04:56.640
<i>He doesn't offer a kind hand 
to anyone, at any time.</i>

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:59.260
<i>Ryu-san can manage that.</i>

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:02.250
<i>It's the sort of kindness that 
makes people better.</i>

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.850
Hmph...

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:10.290
Then, Chiaki-sensei was tricking us.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:13.110
He pretends to be a nice slacker,

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:15.660
but actually, he's scary. That's really bad.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.280
I'm kind of disappointed!

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:18.820
That's not—

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:20.560
That isn't right!

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:25.040
When he's mad, he gets mad!

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:27.080
Sakuraba?

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.770
No matter how nice you are,

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:32.580
if a child does something really wrong,

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:35.260
I think a grown-up's job is to scold them.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:40.180
Sakura! You're so right!

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:42.900
I think so, too!

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.320
I'm so impressed by Chiaki-sensei!

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:47.030
Kakiuchi!

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.940
I like that he's always funny 
and fun to be around.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:53.450
But I thought he wasn't really 
serious about his job...

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:55.820
I guess he is, though.

00:05:56.150 --> 00:06:01.120
I kind of love the gap between his 
normal self and how stern he looks.

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:03.410
How bold!

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:04.410
Just a little.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:06.630
Wait until you graduate!

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:08.120
You startled me!

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:18.570
Such wonderful children, yes?

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:23.480
The aura that filled that 
hallway entranced me.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:24.190
Yeah.

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:28.340
When you see a different side of 
someone than you expected,

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:35.950
whether you see that as positive or 
negative reflects a lot on yourself.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:41.120
In that sense, those girls 
were very noble people.

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:42.620
Right?

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:45.040
I want to be like that!

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:49.410
But you know, that doesn't work...

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:50.860
It doesn't.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.540
You are being tested, yes?

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:05.780
Let's eat!

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:11.150
The texture of these eggs is tremendous!

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:14.560
It's the best part about 
eating pregnant sweetfish.

00:07:16.070 --> 00:07:19.690
And this sweetfish shiokara is just amazing!

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:24.580
The last course is rice, cooked in 
dried sweetfish broth in a clay pot?

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:27.310
Banzai!

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:28.870
Cheers!

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:39.360
You're back?

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:41.260
My school's on a break from exams.

00:07:41.590 --> 00:07:44.690
Same here! Me, too!

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:45.900
Then...

00:07:46.280 --> 00:07:48.340
If you listen in class,

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:50.310
you don't need to cram, right?

00:07:50.310 --> 00:07:52.570
<i>Th-This guy...</i>

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:59.300
Cheating with a smartphone, huh?

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:03.580
Normally, your parents would be 
called, and you'd be suspended.

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:07.210
But it'll be more than that.

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:09.820
Yeah.

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:15.050
It's a bit too big of a deal to 
blame on only one person.

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:19.260
Then, what's going to happen?

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:22.730
One possibility is a general assembly.

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:25.410
A general assembly?

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:33.100
It's over!

00:08:33.100 --> 00:08:36.030
No more... My head is empty.

00:08:36.730 --> 00:08:38.780
Hey, take your seats.

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:47.770
<i>Chiaki... looks worse than yesterday.</i>

00:08:48.450 --> 00:08:50.660
<i>Well, yesterday was rough.</i>

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:54.590
I'd like to start by congratulating 
you on finishing your exams...

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:58.000
But that won't be happening.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:00.680
We're about to have a general assembly.

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:03.420
A general assembly?

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:06.100
Everyone, head to the auditorium immediately.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:08.740
Hase was right.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:16.810
What do you think Yushi-kun's 
school is up to?

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:19.570
Maybe they really are having 
a general assembly.

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:23.380
Hey! I wanna go see!

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:25.780
It's a page in the life of a youth!

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:27.000
Me, too!

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.700
Well, you could go take a little look.

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:33.840
It wouldn't hurt.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.660
Seems fine to me.

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:38.690
Yay!

00:09:57.270 --> 00:10:01.270
Everyone, the general assembly 
is about to begin.

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:07.280
President Kamiya is so cool!

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:09.500
<b>Joutou Business</b>

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:23.760
So tired.

00:10:27.620 --> 00:10:32.640
You all know why we're having a 
general assembly today, right?

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:36.310
During midterms, a smartphone 
was used to cheat.

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:41.820
I'll remind everyone that our school does 
not allow cellphones on the premises.

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:46.170
But doing daily searches isn't practical.

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:50.260
So I overlooked it, as long 
as everyone behaved.

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:55.040
I didn't expect to be betrayed like this.

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:56.160
And I'm not happy!

00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:02.800
<i>Nishiyama...</i>

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:06.970
I was a fool to trust you and spoil you!

00:11:07.280 --> 00:11:10.140
From now on, I will be extremely 
strict about phones.

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:13.560
If I must, I'll conduct searches 
at the school gates.

00:11:15.170 --> 00:11:17.640
If anyone still breaks the rules...

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:21.060
I'll do this.

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:28.810
How awful!

00:11:28.810 --> 00:11:30.430
Did he have to go that far?

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:33.340
That's bold.

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:35.300
Chiaki-chan...

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:42.170
Chiaki-sensei, you're going too far.

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:46.810
So that's the Maid of Orléans, huh?

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:48.840
This is gonna be fun!

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:54.510
When you speak, please think more 
about each student's feelings.

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:56.970
That's right!

00:11:56.970 --> 00:11:57.810
You're going too far!

00:11:57.810 --> 00:11:59.160
What makes you think you're so important?

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:00.350
Come on...

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:03.170
We weren't the ones who cheated!

00:12:03.170 --> 00:12:05.850
That's right! This isn't our problem!

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:08.230
The one who did it should 
take responsibility.

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:11.860
Shut up!

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:16.930
Do you think stringing up the 
guy who did it will end this?

00:12:16.930 --> 00:12:19.030
You don't want to take the blame?

00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:20.000
Don't be so spoiled!

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:24.030
This is everyone's problem!

00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:25.920
Think more!

00:12:29.630 --> 00:12:33.480
Chiaki-sensei, please don't be so harsh.

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:35.870
You'll hurt the children.

00:12:36.300 --> 00:12:39.680
As an educator, can't you show 
more consideration?

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:41.090
That's right!

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:42.320
I'm hurt!

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:43.110
Apologize!

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:47.810
Apologize!

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:52.750
Everyone, let's all talk more peacefully.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:53.660
Okay?

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:55.280
Leave this to me.

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:56.500
Aoki-sensei,

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.830
this is none of your business!

00:13:00.970 --> 00:13:03.540
How can you say that to Aoki-sensei?

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:04.800
We won't let you!

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:07.760
We won't let you talk to 
Aoki-sensei that way.

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:09.520
Apologize.

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:10.680
That's right!

00:13:10.830 --> 00:13:12.480
Apologize!

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:14.510
Apologize!

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:18.300
Apologize! Apologize!

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:22.030
Apologize! Apologize!

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:20.390
<i>Jeez...</i>

00:13:20.850 --> 00:13:24.110
<i>This is the result of your 
irresponsible kindness.</i>

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:26.090
Apologize! Apologize!

00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:26.080
<i>What will you do about this?</i>

00:13:26.230 --> 00:13:29.870
Apologize! Apologize!

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:31.450
Apologize!

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:45.380
<i>Apologize! Apologize!</i>

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:47.940
Okay, it's getting good!

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:51.180
<i>Apologize! Apologize! Apologize!</i>

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:51.170
At this point, no one will 
listen to anything he says.

00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:53.940
They're just letting themselves go crazy!

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:57.060
<i>Apologize! Apologize! Apologize!</i>

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:57.050
They're all so young. So young!

00:13:57.440 --> 00:14:00.840
Ruriko-san, more beer!

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:03.190
<i>Apologize! Apologize! Apologize!</i>

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:02.470
Some salted peanuts, too!

00:14:02.470 --> 00:14:05.900
Now, who will end this? And how?

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:09.070
<i>Apologize! Apologize! Apologize!</i>

00:14:06.340 --> 00:14:09.070
<i>Now, what will you do, Inaba?</i>

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:11.490
<i>Apologize!</i>

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:15.200
Apologize! Apologize!

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:16.070
<i>At this rate, this will turn into a mess!</i>

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:21.130
Apologize! Apologize! Apologize!

00:14:16.730 --> 00:14:19.180
<i>But what do I do?</i>

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:20.790
Master!

00:14:21.240 --> 00:14:23.280
Time to use the Petits!

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:27.300
Apologize! Apologize! Apologize!

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:24.630
The Petits?

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:33.140
Apologize! Apologize! Apologize!

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:30.510
<i>A microphone...</i>

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:31.800
<i>That's right!</i>

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.180
Go, Fool!

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:35.550
On it!

00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:50.860
Yay!

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:54.520
I see! If he does that, no one will notice him!

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:56.880
Yushi-kun's grown up!

00:14:58.480 --> 00:14:59.280
All right.

00:15:03.990 --> 00:15:07.000
Everyone, sit back down in your rows.

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:09.730
Sit!

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:14.870
P-President Kamiya...

00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:21.550
Chiaki-sensei. Aoki-sensei.

00:15:22.010 --> 00:15:25.470
Both of you, please refrain 
from getting emotional.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:33.230
Kamiya-san's so cool!

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:35.270
Chiaki-sensei,

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:40.790
I apologize for betraying the teachers' trust

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:42.980
in the worst way possible.

00:15:44.950 --> 00:15:48.410
Even if smartphones are banned entirely, 
we cannot not complain.

00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:51.270
But please...

00:15:51.270 --> 00:15:53.750
From now on, we promise to 
maintain good behavior.

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:57.540
So please allow us to continue bringing them.

00:15:57.960 --> 00:16:01.550
And please don't break our phones!

00:16:17.270 --> 00:16:18.440
Very well.

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:24.910
There's no way I can completely 
stop people from bringing them.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:27.570
Poor behavior will result 
in confiscation of phones,

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:29.580
to be returned upon graduation.

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:31.050
Graduation?

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:32.290
That's too long...

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:34.760
Please! Three days!

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:38.060
Hey, that's lowering it too much.

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:40.310
I know it's asking a lot.

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:41.470
Please.

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:43.090
Please, Sensei!

00:16:43.090 --> 00:16:44.380
We'll be good!

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:46.720
But you know...

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:49.060
I'm already letting you bring them.

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:52.140
Hmm... Six months.

00:16:52.140 --> 00:16:52.980
A week!

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:54.860
I can't go that far.

00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:56.490
Two weeks, then.

00:16:56.880 --> 00:16:57.690
How about it?

00:16:57.690 --> 00:16:59.730
No, too soon.

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:00.700
Go!

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:02.240
President Kamiya!

00:17:02.240 --> 00:17:13.400
Kamiya! Kamiya! Kamiya!

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:18.710
Kamiya! Kamiya! Kamiya!

00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:18.710
Three months.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:19.970
A month!

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:24.510
Fine! One month!

00:17:24.510 --> 00:17:26.050
Yay!

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:26.860
We won!

00:17:26.860 --> 00:17:28.500
Yay!

00:17:29.220 --> 00:17:32.100
Thank you, Chiaki-sensei.

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:33.470
Listen.

00:17:33.470 --> 00:17:35.510
This is your last chance.

00:17:35.510 --> 00:17:40.530
Once more, and I'll ban and confiscate
 them until graduation.

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:43.580
And no one wants to lose 
their phone for a month.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:45.580
Everyone, you can obey that, right?

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:54.560
That was so mean, master...

00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:55.590
Sorry.

00:17:55.590 --> 00:17:57.210
It was the only thing I could think of.

00:17:57.210 --> 00:17:59.180
I was going to do my best, too...

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:00.630
Anyway, Fool,

00:18:00.630 --> 00:18:01.860
this is amazing!

00:18:01.860 --> 00:18:03.450
Everyone came together!

00:18:03.450 --> 00:18:04.550
Indeed.

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:07.470
"Shut the door in the face," yes?

00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:12.310
"Shut the door in the face."

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:14.930
It's a type of psychological manipulation.

00:18:15.760 --> 00:18:16.980
What do you mean?

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:20.190
You start off with a demanding offer,

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:22.660
to get someone to the line you really wanted.

00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:25.920
He deliberately destroyed that phone.

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:28.860
He started by showing how harsh he was,

00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:31.850
then instituted even harsher conditions,

00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:34.920
to make them think things 
were as bad as possible.

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:38.500
Then he gradually compromised,

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:43.420
so everyone accepted it as better 
than things currently were.

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:40.680
Cheers!

00:18:43.730 --> 00:18:45.840
In the first place,

00:18:45.840 --> 00:18:48.840
he never cared about how 
long he kept the phones.

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:50.840
That is how it is.

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:53.060
I see... I get it.

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:56.440
Chiaki held this general assembly 
because he wanted everyone

00:18:56.440 --> 00:18:59.780
to practice good behavior 
with their smartphones!

00:19:00.440 --> 00:19:01.550
Yes.

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:04.860
His partner, Kamiya-sama, 
did a splendid job, too!

00:19:04.860 --> 00:19:06.120
That's right.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:10.000
But you did wonderfully, as well!

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:11.280
I did?

00:19:11.690 --> 00:19:12.830
Yes!

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:15.240
Not everything went as planned.

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:17.670
Without your quick intervention,

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:21.210
who knows if things would 
have gone this well?

00:19:21.210 --> 00:19:22.440
Yeah?

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:25.200
I do retain some doubt about 
your methods, though.

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:27.170
I won't do that anymore.

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:31.300
So you can keep bringing 
your phones to school.

00:19:31.930 --> 00:19:34.810
But don't use them in class 
or during club activities.

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:38.240
Only during breaks and after school.

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:40.990
And definitely not while walking.

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:44.280
Anyone who violates this rule will 
lose their phone for a month!

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:45.160
That's all!

00:19:45.430 --> 00:19:47.340
Thank you, Sensei!

00:19:47.800 --> 00:19:49.370
Chiaki-sensei!

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:50.490
Great!

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:53.250
Well done, student council president!

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:15.940
Chiaki-sensei and President Kamiya?

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:19.820
That was pretty exciting, chirp.

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:22.190
An afternoon spectacle, chirp!

00:20:22.190 --> 00:20:24.290
I want to see a battle scene next, chirp.

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:25.620
Chirpity-chirp! Chirp!

00:20:29.070 --> 00:20:31.950
Jeez, Chiaki's so annoying...

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:34.580
Who the hell breaks someone's 
phone like that?

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:37.880
He's just controlling us with 
violence and authority!

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:40.710
He's acting too differently than usual.

00:20:41.030 --> 00:20:42.790
He's just a show-off.

00:20:43.020 --> 00:20:44.630
Obnoxious!

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:46.010
Master...

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:51.680
Maybe having everyone understand 
is only an ideal.

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:56.860
Taking action always means 
getting a reaction.

00:20:57.440 --> 00:21:02.320
It cannot be all good or all bad.

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:08.610
When he did this, Chiaki-sama knew 
he might be misunderstood.

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:12.260
There is no reason for it to bother you.

00:21:13.320 --> 00:21:14.530
Yeah.

00:21:15.810 --> 00:21:17.470
<i>But it's frustrating.</i>

00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:22.460
<i>That was how our general assembly ended.</i>

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:25.800
<i>And a new urban legend,</i>

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:30.350
<i>about a glowing bird that flew 
through the hall, was born at JTB.</i>

00:23:10.760 --> 00:23:13.370
After midterms, it's finally 
time for the culture fair.

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:14.310
Let's do this!

00:23:14.310 --> 00:23:15.420
You're all fired-up, huh?

00:23:15.420 --> 00:23:17.640
I remember when I was young...

00:23:17.640 --> 00:23:19.070
Sato-san, you were young?

00:23:19.070 --> 00:23:20.840
Several centuries ago, I think?

00:23:20.840 --> 00:23:23.160
Back then, there were so 
many samurai generals.

00:23:23.160 --> 00:23:24.610
I remember that!

00:23:24.610 --> 00:23:27.000
That would've been in the Sengoku era...

00:23:27.710 --> 00:23:30.630
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:

00:23:30.630 --> 00:23:32.680
Do You Like Other Faces? Or Not?

00:23:30.630 --> 00:23:32.970
<b>Twenty-third Haunting 
Do You Like Other Faces? Or Not?</b>

00:23:32.970 --> 00:23:36.220
Chiaki looks kinda pale. Is he okay?
